            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "NJSS2000"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I usually make something similar to this with Cream of Mushroom soup. I think I prefer the Cream of Celery. Very good."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "thedailygourmet"
            },
            "reviewBody": "If you follow the recipe as written it's going to be extremely bland. I decided to use some sliced butter, onions and sliced mushrooms as well as some Greek seasoning. I sautéed the onions and mushrooms in butter in my instant pot. I placed the pork chops on top of the onion mixture and then sprinkled Greek seasoning over the pork chops. I then poured the soup and milk mixture over the pork chops and cooked it on high pressure for 20 minutes followed by a five-minute natural release and then a quick release. Very tender, and delicious. Served with mashed potatoes and creamed spinach I recipe from AR.",
            "datePublished": "2017-09-20T01:11:26.627Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Rebecca Bassett"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this recipe on the stovetop instead of the oven. I browned pork and onions, and added mushrooms and diced potatoes Lowrys Seasoned salt and pepper. Cooked for 45 mins. on stove top. It is a keeper that way.",
            "datePublished": "2024-07-12T18:44:32.752Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Menwith Hill'er Back Home"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Yummy-licious!!!!!!!!! Will fix this again!!! I made a few changes: I used evaporated milk, instead of regular milk. Also, I added 1 heaping teaspoon of Sylvia's Soul Food Seasoning and 1/2 teaspoon of garlic pepper. Next time I will double the sauce mixture - chop up a pork fillet and cook in the slow cooker - and serve in crusty bread bowls!!!!! Thanks - dinner was fabulous - great recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2004-10-25T11:48:35.340Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SANDRADIFF"
            },
            "reviewBody": "We switched out celery soup and used mushroom soup. Delicious! Served it over rice. Will make this again and highly recommend it. Took 40 minutes.",
            "datePublished": "2012-09-01T19:38:00.413Z"
          },
          {
